;; DEFERRED (split off from simple-error-print-object-method.issue).
;;
;; DEFINE-CONDITION (and DEFCLASS) cannot inherit from a *kernel* condition
;; class.  E.g.:
;;
;;   (define-condition terrible-error (simple-error) ())
;;   => Unhandled SIMPLE-ERROR: DEFCLASS ~S: superclass ~S not found
;;
;; DEFCLASS resolves superclasses only against the CLOS *%classes* registry, but
;; ERROR / SIMPLE-ERROR / SIMPLE-CONDITION / WARNING etc. are kernel classes (not
;; %cls objects), so they are "not found".  To support user condition types that
;; inherit the standard condition hierarchy, DEFCLASS superclass resolution must
;; fall back to the kernel class registry (and the CLOS class must bridge to the
;; kernel CPL so TYPEP / method dispatch keep working).
;;
;; Note: printing of simple-conditions/simple-errors and PRINT-OBJECT methods on
;; condition classes now work (see issues/closed/simple-error-print-object-method).
